<div class="pro-page">

<!-- 1. HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap-wide hero-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">
        <span class="dot-accent"></span>
        WhatCable Pro
      </div>
      <h1>Find the weak link in your <span class="accent">USB-C setup.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">See what the Mac port, cable, dock, adapter and device each support, what was actually negotiated, and where the connection is being limited.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <button class="button accent lg" id="buy-hero">Buy WhatCable Pro for £9.99</button>
        <a href="#features" class="button secondary lg">See what's included</a>
      </div>
      <p class="price-note">One-time purchase, yours permanently. Two Macs. 14-day refund, no questions asked. macOS 14+ on Apple Silicon.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-img">
      <img src="/screenshot-negotiation-diagnostics.webp" alt="WhatCable Pro Negotiation Diagnostics comparing the Mac port, cable and connected device, with the limiting part highlighted">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 2. WHO NEEDS PRO -->
<section class="personas">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-tag">Who needs Pro</span>
      <h2>Who needs Pro</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="personas-grid">
      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-title">Hardware troubleshooting</div>
        <p>A colleague's SSD keeps dropping mid-copy and it's your problem now. Port health counters, event traces, and live power beat guessing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-title">Large cable collections</div>
        <p>Fifteen cables, none labelled. Name each cable, recognise it when it returns, and keep a history of how it performs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-title">Multi-dock setups</div>
        <p>One dock at work, one at home, same laptop, different behaviour. Pro shows what each dock actually negotiated, so you stop blaming the Mac.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-title">High-end docks and displays</div>
        <p>The box said Thunderbolt 4 and 100W. Pro shows what the connection is delivering and which part is setting the limit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 3. THREE FEATURES, STORY-FIRST -->
<section class="story-features">
  <div class="wrap-wide">

    <div class="story-feature">
      <div class="story-feature-text">
        <div class="story-feature-name">Cable history</div>
        <p class="story-feature-setup">Is this the cable that gave me trouble last week?</p>
        <p class="story-feature-explainer">Add a cable, give it a name. WhatCable recognises it next time and builds up a timeline: when you last used it, what it negotiated, whether it has been misbehaving. Saved-cables list, summary per cable, verdict on the port card.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-feature-img">
        <img src="/screenshot-cable-history.webp" alt="Saved Cables screen showing a named Anker Thunderbolt cable with a Performing verdict, last seen one second ago, and History, Rename, and Delete actions" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-feature reverse">
      <div class="story-feature-text">
        <div class="story-feature-name">Negotiation Diagnostics</div>
        <p class="story-feature-setup">You bought a 40Gbps cable and the drive runs at 5.</p>
        <p class="story-feature-explainer">Port, cable, and device side by side against what was actually negotiated, weak link highlighted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-feature-img">
        <img src="/screenshot-negotiation-diagnostics.webp" alt="Negotiation Diagnostics screen showing per-port power and data-speed breakdowns with the bottleneck highlighted" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-feature">
      <div class="story-feature-text">
        <div class="story-feature-name">Display Diagnostics</div>
        <p class="story-feature-setup">The new 4K display is running at 30Hz and macOS won't say why.</p>
        <p class="story-feature-explainer">Your monitor's capability vs what the link is carrying, adapter named. It only says "not the cable" when the evidence shows it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-feature-img">
        <img src="/screenshot-display-diagnostics.webp" alt="Display Diagnostics screen showing a monitor's top mode against what the DisplayPort link is carrying, with the adapter named and the shortfall highlighted" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-feature reverse">
      <div class="story-feature-text">
        <div class="story-feature-name">Port Diagnostics</div>
        <p class="story-feature-setup">The drive keeps dropping out, but never while you are watching.</p>
        <p class="story-feature-explainer">Per-port counters that keep score when you are not there: attaches, detaches, hard resets, failed role swaps, VDO failures. Alongside them, the live power contract, the PD event log, pin-level signal routing, and liquid-detection state.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="story-feature-img">
        <img src="/screenshot-diagnostics.webp" alt="Port Diagnostics screen showing port health counters with 27 attaches and 40 VDO failures flagged, liquid detection state, and the live power contract with its active request and the charger's source PDOs" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- 4. REVIEWS -->
<section class="quotes-strip" aria-label="What reviewers and users said">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-tag">Reviews</span>
      <h2>What reviewers said.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="quotes-grid">
      <figure class="pull-quote">
        <blockquote class="quote">A tiny app that does one thing, does it well.</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="attribution">Dwight Silverman, Houston Chronicle</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <a class="pull-quote" href="https://lifehacker.com/tech/whatcable-mac-app" rel="noopener">
        <blockquote class="quote">WhatCable does a fine job of analyzing the cables attached to your Mac.</blockquote>
        <span class="attribution">David Nield, Lifehacker</span>
      </a>
      <a class="pull-quote" href="https://www.makeuseof.com/this-free-app-tells-me-exactly-what-my-usb-cables-can-do/" rel="noopener">
        <blockquote class="quote">Finally tells you what your USB-C cables can actually do.</blockquote>
        <span class="attribution">Brady Snyder, MakeUseOf</span>
